Sent: Wednesday, September 23, 2026 12:59 PM
To: Complaints, Whistleblower (Wyden); media.portland@fbi.gov; oig.hotline@=
usdoj.gov
Cc: evan.meyers@lanecountyor.gov; matthew.j.oliver@usda.gov; jake.hyde@osp.=
oregon.gov; jerred.nelson@osp.oregon.gov; sean.henderson@osp.oregon.gov; ha=
ley.mcquillan@osp.oregon.gov; Kyle.Kennedy@osp.oregon.gov; jehyde@fbi.gov; =
rclong@fbi.gov; jrussell6@fbi.gov; Dianne.Greenlee@doj.oregon.gov; oprc.pub=
liccomment@oprd.oregon.gov; risk.management@das.oregon.gov; Governor Kotek =
* GOV
Subject: Federal task force resources in a state matter with no criminal pr=
edicate

Senator Wyden,
Attached is my letter of September 23, 2026.
An Oregon State Police detective who also serves as a task force officer wi=
th the Portland FBI Joint Terrorism Task Force distributed my name to FBI p=
ersonnel, then moved my driver's record and a report about me from his FBI =
account into a state case file he had declared, in writing two days earlier=
, was not an FBI case. The matter never had a criminal predicate. The state=
's own file closed with "there is no evidence White has committed any crime=
s."
I am asking what authority permitted the March 13, 2026 transfer, what the =
FBI created and retains about me, and who audits the movement of informatio=
n across the state-federal seam by dual-role officers.
I am your constituent. Every fact in the letter is cited to the Oregon Stat=
e Police production of September 3, 2026, which is public in full at oprdvo=
lunteerabuse.org.
Respectfully submitted,
Robert Samuel White
P.O. Box 334, Reedsport, Oregon 97467


--_000_33ab39d2d635424ab673fb357837f16cwydensenategov_
